1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,700
學 (xué). To learn, in Chinese…

2
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:07,990
Look closely:
this character hides two hands.

3
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:10,470
Today, no one sees them anymore.

4
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:11,860
Where did they go?

5
00:00:12,093 --> 00:00:15,243
In modern Chinese, it takes eight strokes.

6
00:00:15,293 --> 00:00:17,393
It once took sixteen.

7
00:00:17,453 --> 00:00:21,643
Between the two:
three thousand years, an emperor,

8
00:00:21,693 --> 00:00:23,043
a dictionary…

9
00:00:23,093 --> 00:00:25,713
and two hands fading away.

10
00:00:25,853 --> 00:00:29,753
To find them, we must go back to
the first person who drew it.

11
00:00:30,195 --> 00:00:35,455
Around twelve hundred and fifty BC,
in Anyang 安阳, capital of the Shang 商.

12
00:00:35,715 --> 00:00:40,065
The diviners press a red-hot
bronze rod to a turtle shell.

13
00:00:40,115 --> 00:00:44,945
It cracks. In the crack,
they read the answer of the ancestors…

14
00:00:44,995 --> 00:00:46,415
then they carve it.

15
00:00:46,835 --> 00:00:49,185
This is where our sign appears.

16
00:00:49,235 --> 00:00:52,785
At its center, crossed sticks: yáo 爻.

17
00:00:52,835 --> 00:00:54,465
Below, a roof.

18
00:00:54,515 --> 00:00:55,945
And on either side…

19
00:00:55,995 --> 00:00:58,625
two hands, reaching for the sticks.

20
00:00:58,675 --> 00:01:01,775
Hands that count, show, handle.

21
00:01:02,115 --> 00:01:05,855
And yet, under this roof,
someone is missing.

22
00:01:11,165 --> 00:01:13,785
Two centuries later come the Zhou 周.

23
00:01:14,125 --> 00:01:18,795
Their inscriptions are no longer
carved in bone, but cast in bronze,

24
00:01:18,845 --> 00:01:21,545
deep inside great ritual vessels.

25
00:01:22,045 --> 00:01:26,665
And under the roof,
a newcomer slips in: a child.

26
00:01:26,845 --> 00:01:29,595
This time, the sign says it all.

27
00:01:29,645 --> 00:01:33,385
Hands passing on,
under a roof, to a child.

28
00:01:33,965 --> 00:01:38,235
On one vessel, a king has
archery taught to young nobles…

29
00:01:38,285 --> 00:01:40,105
in the hall of study.

30
00:01:44,014 --> 00:01:46,604
Two hundred and twenty-one BC.

31
00:01:46,654 --> 00:01:49,794
The First Emperor unifies China.

32
00:01:50,014 --> 00:01:54,524
Until then, the same word wore a
different face in every kingdom.

33
00:01:54,574 --> 00:01:59,964
His minister, Li Si 李斯,
imposes one script: the small seal.

34
00:02:00,014 --> 00:02:01,884
The curves grow long.

35
00:02:01,934 --> 00:02:05,084
Everything aligns, in perfect symmetry.

36
00:02:05,134 --> 00:02:07,244
The two hands are still there.

37
00:02:07,294 --> 00:02:08,314
For now.

38
00:02:08,656 --> 00:02:14,606
Around the year one hundred, under the Han
汉, a scholar takes on an immense task.

39
00:02:14,656 --> 00:02:17,516
To explain the shape of every character.

40
00:02:17,936 --> 00:02:19,756
His name is Xu Shen 许慎.

41
00:02:19,936 --> 00:02:25,436
His book, the Shuowen Jiezi 说文解字,
analyses over nine thousand.

42
00:02:25,696 --> 00:02:30,766
There our sign gets its definition:
to learn is to awaken.

43
00:02:30,816 --> 00:02:31,886
And the roof?

44
00:02:31,936 --> 00:02:34,796
The darkness that still covers the mind.

45
00:02:35,163 --> 00:02:39,993
Meanwhile, in the offices of the empire,
the scribes write fast.

46
00:02:40,043 --> 00:02:41,223
Very fast.

47
00:02:41,563 --> 00:02:44,663
The brush flattens curves, cuts loops.

48
00:02:44,923 --> 00:02:48,583
The two hands freeze into a square block,
like a mortar.

49
00:02:49,003 --> 00:02:50,663
Their meaning fades.

50
00:02:51,003 --> 00:02:55,703
The regular script finally fixes the form:
sixteen strokes.

51
00:02:56,043 --> 00:02:58,383
Sixteen strokes is a lot.

52
00:02:58,523 --> 00:03:04,823
Copy after copy, the hurried hand shrinks
the whole top to three little strokes…

53
00:03:06,303 --> 00:03:08,813
The hands were not erased by decree.

54
00:03:08,863 --> 00:03:13,563
They were erased by other hands:
those of hurried scribes.

55
00:03:19,598 --> 00:03:25,468
In the twentieth century, Japan, then
China, officially adopt this short form.

56
00:03:25,518 --> 00:03:27,098
Eight strokes.

57
00:03:27,278 --> 00:03:32,268
So the brush starts again:
sticks to count, a roof to shelter,

58
00:03:32,318 --> 00:03:35,868
two hands to show, a child to receive.

59
00:03:35,918 --> 00:03:39,788
And so 學 (xué) is born: to learn.

60
00:03:39,838 --> 00:03:43,708
Today it stands at the gate
of every school, xuéxiào 學校.

61
00:03:43,758 --> 00:03:49,948
It opens xuésheng 學生, the student,
and closes dàxué 大學, the university.

62
00:03:49,998 --> 00:03:53,708
To recognize it:
three little strokes, a roof…

63
00:03:53,758 --> 00:03:56,538
and beneath, always, the child.

64
00:03:56,930 --> 00:03:59,310
The hands have faded from the sign.

65
00:03:59,650 --> 00:04:01,200
Not from the gesture.

66
00:04:01,250 --> 00:04:07,230
For three thousand years, to learn has
meant to receive what other hands pass on.

67
00:04:07,410 --> 00:04:11,550
These sticks and this child appear
again in another character.

68
00:04:11,810 --> 00:04:13,160
But this time…

69
00:04:13,210 --> 00:04:15,310
the hand holds a rod.
